[{:question/id #uuid "2564c8e6-dd58-5512-bb79-d13a805cc112" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/problem "Evaluate the integral of the function $f(x,y)=x$ along the line $y=2 x,$ $\\,0\\le x\\le 3.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve is of the form $y=y(x).$ Therefore, by setting $x=t,$ we have $y=y(t)=2 t.$ This gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle t,2 t\\rangle,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le 3\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm dx}{\\mathrm dt}\\mathbf i+\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dt}\\mathbf j \\\\ &=\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}(t)\\mathbf i+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}(2 t)\\mathbf j \\\\ &=\\mathbf i+(2)\\mathbf j \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(\\frac{\\mathrm dx}{\\mathrm dt})^2+(\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dt})^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{1^2+(2)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm ds&=\\int_{0}^{3}f(r(t))\\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{3}(t)(\\sqrt{5})\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\left[\\frac{\\sqrt{5} t^{2}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{3} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\left((3)^{2}-(0)^{2}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\left(9-0\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{9 \\sqrt{5}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "17a59230-cdc0-59cf-8d49-a7d059d179cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8160d239-5719-5314-9b34-25360242df8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id "a-8160d239-5719-5314-9b34-25360242df8b"} {:answer/id #uuid "c98eda7f-7904-59d5-aed5-f095f55995d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- \\frac{9 \\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/id "a-c98eda7f-7904-59d5-aed5-f095f55995d0"} {:answer/id #uuid "b72aa66a-4ae8-5eb8-a19d-10e8556f0769" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id "a-b72aa66a-4ae8-5eb8-a19d-10e8556f0769"} {:answer/id #uuid "f3f6bd32-8ed5-5aec-826d-0d30d73baf91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9 \\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/id "a-f3f6bd32-8ed5-5aec-826d-0d30d73baf91"} {:answer/id #uuid "9618b0be-10e0-54af-bddc-144790bcb25d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{45}{2}" :db/id "a-9618b0be-10e0-54af-bddc-144790bcb25d"}] :answer-field/correct "a-f3f6bd32-8ed5-5aec-826d-0d30d73baf91" :db/id "f-17a59230-cdc0-59cf-8d49-a7d059d179cb"}] :db/id "q-2564c8e6-dd58-5512-bb79-d13a805cc112"} [:db/add 17592186152158 :knowledge-point/questions "q-2564c8e6-dd58-5512-bb79-d13a805cc112"] [:db/ensure "q-2564c8e6-dd58-5512-bb79-d13a805cc112" :question/validate] [:db/ensure "f-17a59230-cdc0-59cf-8d49-a7d059d179cb" :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure "a-8160d239-5719-5314-9b34-25360242df8b" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-c98eda7f-7904-59d5-aed5-f095f55995d0" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-b72aa66a-4ae8-5eb8-a19d-10e8556f0769" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-f3f6bd32-8ed5-5aec-826d-0d30d73baf91" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-9618b0be-10e0-54af-bddc-144790bcb25d" :answer/validate] {:question/id #uuid "fa2eae58-23f0-53d8-954b-616c559e82a9" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/problem "Evaluate the integral of the function $f(x,y)=2 x$ along the line $y=3 x,$ $\\,0\\le x\\le 4.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve is of the form $y=y(x).$ Therefore, by setting $x=t,$ we have $y=y(t)=3 t.$ This gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle t,3 t\\rangle,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le 4\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm dx}{\\mathrm dt}\\mathbf i+\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dt}\\mathbf j \\\\ &=\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}(t)\\mathbf i+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}(3 t)\\mathbf j \\\\ &=\\mathbf i+(3)\\mathbf j \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(\\frac{\\mathrm dx}{\\mathrm dt})^2+(\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dt})^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{1^2+(3)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=2 x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=2 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm ds&=\\int_{0}^{4}f(r(t))\\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{4}(2 t)(\\sqrt{10})\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\left[\\sqrt{10} t^{2}\\right]_{0}^{4} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{10}\\left((4)^{2}-(0)^{2}\\right) \\\\ &=\\sqrt{10}\\left(16-0\\right) \\\\ &=16 \\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "7d7d77a5-ca55-5835-beb8-b8509e3fef56" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c0613bc-32a4-53a2-a943-9e50b992e369" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16 \\sqrt{10}" :db/id "a-4c0613bc-32a4-53a2-a943-9e50b992e369"} {:answer/id #uuid "867db4e2-70dd-5f07-8dc4-522fdb1b0abe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/id "a-867db4e2-70dd-5f07-8dc4-522fdb1b0abe"} {:answer/id #uuid "b4af4815-a8ff-5192-b441-27ae750e4043" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "160" :db/id "a-b4af4815-a8ff-5192-b441-27ae750e4043"} {:answer/id #uuid "5fa57f44-2642-593c-a3e7-ef6c93fe59eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- 16 \\sqrt{10}" :db/id "a-5fa57f44-2642-593c-a3e7-ef6c93fe59eb"} {:answer/id #uuid "0d630ca6-fd28-58ed-995a-8da968fd5ba9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8 \\sqrt{10}" :db/id "a-0d630ca6-fd28-58ed-995a-8da968fd5ba9"}] :answer-field/correct "a-4c0613bc-32a4-53a2-a943-9e50b992e369" :db/id "f-7d7d77a5-ca55-5835-beb8-b8509e3fef56"}] :db/id "q-fa2eae58-23f0-53d8-954b-616c559e82a9"} [:db/add 17592186152158 :knowledge-point/questions "q-fa2eae58-23f0-53d8-954b-616c559e82a9"] [:db/ensure "q-fa2eae58-23f0-53d8-954b-616c559e82a9" :question/validate] [:db/ensure "f-7d7d77a5-ca55-5835-beb8-b8509e3fef56" :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure "a-4c0613bc-32a4-53a2-a943-9e50b992e369" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-867db4e2-70dd-5f07-8dc4-522fdb1b0abe" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-b4af4815-a8ff-5192-b441-27ae750e4043" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-5fa57f44-2642-593c-a3e7-ef6c93fe59eb" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-0d630ca6-fd28-58ed-995a-8da968fd5ba9" :answer/validate] {:question/id #uuid "6ab95a8c-ac51-5396-919b-6a451ca13ac6" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/problem "Evaluate the integral of the function $f(x,y)=3 x$ along the line $y=4 x,$ $\\,0\\le x\\le 5.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve is of the form $y=y(x).$ Therefore, by setting $x=t,$ we have $y=y(t)=4 t.$ This gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle t,4 t\\rangle,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le 5\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm dx}{\\mathrm dt}\\mathbf i+\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dt}\\mathbf j \\\\ &=\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}(t)\\mathbf i+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}(4 t)\\mathbf j \\\\ &=\\mathbf i+(4)\\mathbf j \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(\\frac{\\mathrm dx}{\\mathrm dt})^2+(\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dt})^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{1^2+(4)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{17}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=3 x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=3 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm ds&=\\int_{0}^{5}f(r(t))\\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{5}(3 t)(\\sqrt{17})\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\left[\\frac{3 \\sqrt{17} t^{2}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{5} \\\\ &=\\frac{3 \\sqrt{17}}{2}\\left((5)^{2}-(0)^{2}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{3 \\sqrt{17}}{2}\\left(25-0\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{75 \\sqrt{17}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "4b9afa8e-4db7-5a3a-a384-3177ceb89729" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0e57f6d-ff24-5498-8177-a14094d5bd2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{75 \\sqrt{17}}{2}" :db/id "a-a0e57f6d-ff24-5498-8177-a14094d5bd2b"} {:answer/id #uuid "cc301a85-6415-5f5a-a1ec-c9814b9c754e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- \\frac{75 \\sqrt{17}}{2}" :db/id "a-cc301a85-6415-5f5a-a1ec-c9814b9c754e"} {:answer/id #uuid "bbc6fca7-a70d-5ad4-b81d-03df2ea33f55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{75}{2}" :db/id "a-bbc6fca7-a70d-5ad4-b81d-03df2ea33f55"} {:answer/id #uuid "0e40f44d-615f-5865-a602-f53e98d24e9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15 \\sqrt{17}" :db/id "a-0e40f44d-615f-5865-a602-f53e98d24e9b"} {:answer/id #uuid "65d7c7ed-cf67-5d74-9d2d-7d230e621f18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1275}{2}" :db/id "a-65d7c7ed-cf67-5d74-9d2d-7d230e621f18"}] :answer-field/correct "a-a0e57f6d-ff24-5498-8177-a14094d5bd2b" :db/id "f-4b9afa8e-4db7-5a3a-a384-3177ceb89729"}] :db/id "q-6ab95a8c-ac51-5396-919b-6a451ca13ac6"} [:db/add 17592186152158 :knowledge-point/questions "q-6ab95a8c-ac51-5396-919b-6a451ca13ac6"] [:db/ensure "q-6ab95a8c-ac51-5396-919b-6a451ca13ac6" :question/validate] [:db/ensure "f-4b9afa8e-4db7-5a3a-a384-3177ceb89729" :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure "a-a0e57f6d-ff24-5498-8177-a14094d5bd2b" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-cc301a85-6415-5f5a-a1ec-c9814b9c754e" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-bbc6fca7-a70d-5ad4-b81d-03df2ea33f55" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-0e40f44d-615f-5865-a602-f53e98d24e9b" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-65d7c7ed-cf67-5d74-9d2d-7d230e621f18" :answer/validate] {:question/id #uuid "969d5e52-a658-5dd3-9654-fc884ce1b67b" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/problem "Evaluate the integral of the function $f(x,y)=4 x$ along the line $y=5 x,$ $\\,0\\le x\\le 6.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve is of the form $y=y(x).$ Therefore, by setting $x=t,$ we have $y=y(t)=5 t.$ This gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle t,5 t\\rangle,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le 6\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm dx}{\\mathrm dt}\\mathbf i+\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dt}\\mathbf j \\\\ &=\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}(t)\\mathbf i+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}(5 t)\\mathbf j \\\\ &=\\mathbf i+(5)\\mathbf j \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(\\frac{\\mathrm dx}{\\mathrm dt})^2+(\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dt})^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{1^2+(5)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{26}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=4 x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=4 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm ds&=\\int_{0}^{6}f(r(t))\\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{6}(4 t)(\\sqrt{26})\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\left[2 \\sqrt{26} t^{2}\\right]_{0}^{6} \\\\ &=2 \\sqrt{26}\\left((6)^{2}-(0)^{2}\\right) \\\\ &=2 \\sqrt{26}\\left(36-0\\right) \\\\ &=72 \\sqrt{26}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "49a0cf1d-2ab0-543e-9e64-7b0edf5e8453" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a75de59-ff24-5015-82fd-549b0eabf5f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- 72 \\sqrt{26}" :db/id "a-6a75de59-ff24-5015-82fd-549b0eabf5f7"} {:answer/id #uuid "77c7a369-2abc-53dd-b2aa-5a817fb5b5bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "72 \\sqrt{26}" :db/id "a-77c7a369-2abc-53dd-b2aa-5a817fb5b5bf"} {:answer/id #uuid "871f3101-6660-58fb-8c35-50aad648b843" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24 \\sqrt{26}" :db/id "a-871f3101-6660-58fb-8c35-50aad648b843"} {:answer/id #uuid "482b716c-5732-5534-84fd-923827a99c6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1872" :db/id "a-482b716c-5732-5534-84fd-923827a99c6a"} {:answer/id #uuid "8d989555-4656-5801-a461-47d42c1dd876" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "72" :db/id "a-8d989555-4656-5801-a461-47d42c1dd876"}] :answer-field/correct "a-77c7a369-2abc-53dd-b2aa-5a817fb5b5bf" :db/id "f-49a0cf1d-2ab0-543e-9e64-7b0edf5e8453"}] :db/id "q-969d5e52-a658-5dd3-9654-fc884ce1b67b"} [:db/add 17592186152158 :knowledge-point/questions "q-969d5e52-a658-5dd3-9654-fc884ce1b67b"] [:db/ensure "q-969d5e52-a658-5dd3-9654-fc884ce1b67b" :question/validate] [:db/ensure "f-49a0cf1d-2ab0-543e-9e64-7b0edf5e8453" :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure "a-6a75de59-ff24-5015-82fd-549b0eabf5f7" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-77c7a369-2abc-53dd-b2aa-5a817fb5b5bf" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-871f3101-6660-58fb-8c35-50aad648b843" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-482b716c-5732-5534-84fd-923827a99c6a" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-8d989555-4656-5801-a461-47d42c1dd876" :answer/validate] {:question/id #uuid "2eade040-7c90-5638-966c-718b41cfb998" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/problem "Evaluate the integral of the function $f(x,y)=5 x$ along the line $y=6 x,$ $\\,0\\le x\\le 7.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve is of the form $y=y(x).$ Therefore, by setting $x=t,$ we have $y=y(t)=6 t.$ This gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle t,6 t\\rangle,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le 7\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm dx}{\\mathrm dt}\\mathbf i+\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dt}\\mathbf j \\\\ &=\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}(t)\\mathbf i+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}(6 t)\\mathbf j \\\\ &=\\mathbf i+(6)\\mathbf j \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(\\frac{\\mathrm dx}{\\mathrm dt})^2+(\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dt})^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{1^2+(6)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{37}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=5 x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=5 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm ds&=\\int_{0}^{7}f(r(t))\\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{7}(5 t)(\\sqrt{37})\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\left[\\frac{5 \\sqrt{37} t^{2}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{7} \\\\ &=\\frac{5 \\sqrt{37}}{2}\\left((7)^{2}-(0)^{2}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{5 \\sqrt{37}}{2}\\left(49-0\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{245 \\sqrt{37}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "1f81595a-0aec-5788-9a31-df107d898cd3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9544065-9a17-5e0c-a38b-236361697c34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9065}{2}" :db/id "a-f9544065-9a17-5e0c-a38b-236361697c34"} {:answer/id #uuid "224fc2fd-156e-5950-be40-d81695a7789b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{245}{2}" :db/id "a-224fc2fd-156e-5950-be40-d81695a7789b"} {:answer/id #uuid "07329d51-3f5e-5e2e-8441-b2141aff317e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "35 \\sqrt{37}" :db/id "a-07329d51-3f5e-5e2e-8441-b2141aff317e"} {:answer/id #uuid "7105e2b6-33c5-596d-aaf1-e33906b7e9ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- \\frac{245 \\sqrt{37}}{2}" :db/id "a-7105e2b6-33c5-596d-aaf1-e33906b7e9ad"} {:answer/id #uuid "38a9bc69-d00d-5b76-b39d-357b71605439" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{245 \\sqrt{37}}{2}" :db/id "a-38a9bc69-d00d-5b76-b39d-357b71605439"}] :answer-field/correct "a-38a9bc69-d00d-5b76-b39d-357b71605439" :db/id "f-1f81595a-0aec-5788-9a31-df107d898cd3"}] :db/id "q-2eade040-7c90-5638-966c-718b41cfb998"} [:db/add 17592186152158 :knowledge-point/questions "q-2eade040-7c90-5638-966c-718b41cfb998"] [:db/ensure "q-2eade040-7c90-5638-966c-718b41cfb998" :question/validate] [:db/ensure "f-1f81595a-0aec-5788-9a31-df107d898cd3" :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure "a-f9544065-9a17-5e0c-a38b-236361697c34" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-224fc2fd-156e-5950-be40-d81695a7789b" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-07329d51-3f5e-5e2e-8441-b2141aff317e" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-7105e2b6-33c5-596d-aaf1-e33906b7e9ad" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-38a9bc69-d00d-5b76-b39d-357b71605439" :answer/validate] {:question/id #uuid "2bf9d63c-b3f4-5d38-83c5-c18e8598dd9c" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/problem "Evaluate the integral of the function $f(x,y)=x \\left(y - 1\\right)$ along the line $y=2 x + 1,$ $\\,0\\le x\\le 2.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve is of the form $y=y(x).$ Therefore, by setting $x=t,$ we have $y=y(t)=2 t + 1.$ This gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle t,2 t + 1\\rangle,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le 2\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm dx}{\\mathrm dt}\\mathbf i+\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dt}\\mathbf j \\\\ &=\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}(t)\\mathbf i+\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}(2 t + 1)\\mathbf j \\\\ &=\\mathbf i+(2)\\mathbf j \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(\\frac{\\mathrm dx}{\\mathrm dt})^2+(\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dt})^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{1^2+(2)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=x \\left(y - 1\\right)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=2 t^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm ds&=\\int_{0}^{2}f(r(t))\\|\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2}(2 t^{2})(\\sqrt{5})\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\left[\\frac{2 \\sqrt{5} t^{3}}{3}\\right]_{0}^{2} \\\\ &=\\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{3}\\left((2)^{3}-(0)^{3}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{3}\\left(8-0\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{16 \\sqrt{5}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "d538b1dd-c792-572f-8c1f-8353d9802950" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33be0b46-f243-554c-9d9e-964dc5eb30b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id "a-33be0b46-f243-554c-9d9e-964dc5eb30b6"} {:answer/id #uuid "020d5907-9b7b-5719-a1f1-4f44c5409284" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16 \\sqrt{5}}{3}" :db/id "a-020d5907-9b7b-5719-a1f1-4f44c5409284"} {:answer/id #uuid "f8e63c2b-a619-54eb-9772-8aa7f8b9dbf8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- \\frac{16 \\sqrt{5}}{3}" :db/id "a-f8e63c2b-a619-54eb-9772-8aa7f8b9dbf8"} {:answer/id #uuid "c56967e6-dc2a-5dcc-9976-37549a83e6d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id "a-c56967e6-dc2a-5dcc-9976-37549a83e6d7"} {:answer/id #uuid "6c57458e-2426-55cb-b5d8-65aeae4d3130" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{80}{3}" :db/id "a-6c57458e-2426-55cb-b5d8-65aeae4d3130"}] :answer-field/correct "a-020d5907-9b7b-5719-a1f1-4f44c5409284" :db/id "f-d538b1dd-c792-572f-8c1f-8353d9802950"}] :db/id "q-2bf9d63c-b3f4-5d38-83c5-c18e8598dd9c"} [:db/add 17592186152158 :knowledge-point/questions "q-2bf9d63c-b3f4-5d38-83c5-c18e8598dd9c"] [:db/ensure "q-2bf9d63c-b3f4-5d38-83c5-c18e8598dd9c" :question/validate] [:db/ensure "f-d538b1dd-c792-572f-8c1f-8353d9802950" :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure "a-33be0b46-f243-554c-9d9e-964dc5eb30b6" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-020d5907-9b7b-5719-a1f1-4f44c5409284" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-f8e63c2b-a619-54eb-9772-8aa7f8b9dbf8" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-c56967e6-dc2a-5dcc-9976-37549a83e6d7" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-6c57458e-2426-55cb-b5d8-65aeae4d3130" :answer/validate] {:question/id #uuid "74138378-8762-53b8-ac46-3f0ace177732" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/problem "Evaluate the integral of the function $f(x,y)=({x}^{2}+y)$ along the line $y=3x+2,$ $\\,0\\le x\\le 2.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve is of the form $y=y(x).$ Therefore, by setting $x=t,$ we have $y=y(t)=3t+2.$ This gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨t,\\,3t+2⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le 2\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t+2)j \\\\  & =i+3\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & ={t}^{2}+(3t+2)={t}^{2}+3t+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({t}^{2}+3t+2)\\cdot \\sqrt{10}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({t}^{2}+3t+2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}\\,(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{2}+2t){|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}(\\frac{8}{3}+6+4) \\\\  & =\\frac{38 \\sqrt{10}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "d7c75bfe-126d-5238-b88a-6cc39af08281" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c916508-666a-5d4f-bc0e-83237918f953" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{380}{3}" :db/id "a-5c916508-666a-5d4f-bc0e-83237918f953"} {:answer/id #uuid "0b718af0-92d3-59c9-9229-69b2816bd3cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- \\frac{38 \\sqrt{10}}{3}" :db/id "a-0b718af0-92d3-59c9-9229-69b2816bd3cf"} {:answer/id #uuid "53bf3405-0c98-553b-9ce6-af3d6065c7a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{38 \\sqrt{10}}{3}" :db/id "a-53bf3405-0c98-553b-9ce6-af3d6065c7a7"} {:answer/id #uuid "9a892440-907b-5477-a7e0-478061c8676f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10 \\sqrt{10}" :db/id "a-9a892440-907b-5477-a7e0-478061c8676f"} {:answer/id #uuid "5fd61603-c8b6-5e98-acdd-11a2306975c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{38}{3}" :db/id "a-5fd61603-c8b6-5e98-acdd-11a2306975c1"}] :answer-field/correct "a-53bf3405-0c98-553b-9ce6-af3d6065c7a7" :db/id "f-d7c75bfe-126d-5238-b88a-6cc39af08281"}] :db/id "q-74138378-8762-53b8-ac46-3f0ace177732"} [:db/add 17592186152158 :knowledge-point/questions "q-74138378-8762-53b8-ac46-3f0ace177732"] [:db/ensure "q-74138378-8762-53b8-ac46-3f0ace177732" :question/validate] [:db/ensure "f-d7c75bfe-126d-5238-b88a-6cc39af08281" :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure "a-5c916508-666a-5d4f-bc0e-83237918f953" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-0b718af0-92d3-59c9-9229-69b2816bd3cf" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-53bf3405-0c98-553b-9ce6-af3d6065c7a7" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-9a892440-907b-5477-a7e0-478061c8676f" :answer/validate] [:db/ensure "a-5fd61603-c8b6-5e98-acdd-11a2306975c1" :answer/validate] {:question/id #uuid "7e94a1c8-32a5-5aeb-82a3-988f3971786f" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/problem "Evaluate the integral of the function $f(x,y)=2{y}^{2}$ along the curve $y={e}^{x},$ $\\,0\\le x\\le \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve is of the form $y=y(x).$ Therefore, by setting $x=t,$ we have $y=y(t)={e}^{t}.$ This gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨t,\\,{e}^{t}⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})j \\\\  & =i+{e}^{t}j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{({e}^{t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{e}^{2t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=2{y}^{2}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2({e}^{t})^{2}=2{e}^{2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}2{e}^{2t}\\cdot \\sqrt{1+{e}^{2t}}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}2{e}^{2t}\\,\\sqrt{1+{e}^{2t}}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=1+{e}^{2t}$, $\\text{d}u=2{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}2{e}^{2t}\\,\\sqrt{1+{e}^{2t}}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{2}^{17}{u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}{|}_{2}^{17} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}({17}^{3/2}-{2}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(17 \\sqrt{17}-2\\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =- \\frac{4 \\sqrt{2}}{3} + \\frac{34 \\sqrt{17}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "927562b5-720d-53ed-bf92-54fcb887de44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b9920b7-0e21-5c1f-8111-86f228f479e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/id "a-8b9920b7-0e21-5c1f-8111-86f228f479e7"} {:answer/id #uuid "2c2c9bda-2b1c-547d-a80e-eff23e39c06d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- \\frac{4 \\sqrt{2}}{3} + \\frac{34 \\sqrt{17}}{3}" :db/id "a-2c2c9bda-2b1c-547d-a80e-eff23e39c06d"} {:answer/id #uuid "9e06ccd9-0287-543d-9f3b-377e3c903179" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ln{\\left(18446744073709551616 \\right)}" :db/id "a-9e06ccd9-0287-543d-9f3b-377e3c903179"} {:answer/id #uuid "8c2807fa-